 "methodology_html": "<strong>Clusters</strong> group near-duplicate keywords so shared demand is counted once (Google reports close variants at the same volume). <strong>Volume</strong> = deduped Miami-metro search demand + the explicit \u201c[service] [city]\u201d searches across the 15 priority suburbs (only Hialeah clears Keyword Planner\u2019s threshold \u2014 explicit suburb search is thin; the suburb pages mainly capture proximity searches). <strong>Current traffic</strong> = real GSC clicks/mo today. <strong>Potential traffic</strong> = volume \u00d7 a 20-40% top-3 click-through (graded by intent), and the <strong>gain</strong> nets out what the cluster already earns. <strong>New leads</strong> = gained clicks \u00d7 2.0% (conservative \u2014 site-blended is 0.8%, commercial-rental pages run 3-5%). Leads count form_submit + contact_form_submit only; phone, email and GBP\u2192site clicks are tracked separately."
